{
  "info": {
    "name": "Mini Project 2 — Saipul AI2",
    "description": "Two data pipelines, one API.\n\n**Path A (ETL):** Scraped articles → cleaned → loaded\n**Path B (ELT):** Raw CSV → loaded → SQL transforms\n\n## Setup\n1. Set `base_url` variable (default: http://localhost:8000)\n2. Run \"Get JWT Token\" first — it auto-saves the token\n3. All protected endpoints use API Key by default\n4. Switch to Bearer token in the JWT folder\n\n## Auth Methods\n- **API Key:** X-API-Key header\n- **JWT Bearer:** POST /token → use access_token",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "http://localhost:8000",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "api_key",
      "value": "CHANGE_ME_API_KEY",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "client_id",
      "value": "saipul_client",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "client_secret",
      "value": "CHANGE_ME_CLIENT_SECRET",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "jwt_token",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "filter_source",
      "value": "bbc",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "date_from",
      "value": "2026-01-01",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Mini Project 2 — Required endpoints",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "01 Search default",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{api_key}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/articles/search"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Default pagination', () => { pm.expect(j.page).to.eql(1); pm.expect(j.per_page).to.eql(10); pm.expect(j.total_pages).to.eql(Math.ceil(j.total_items / j.per_page)); });",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('page1_ids', JSON.stringify(j.data.map(x => x.id)));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "02 Search source + date",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{api_key}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/articles/search?source={{filter_source}}&date_from={{date_from}}"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Source filter', () => j.data.forEach(x => pm.expect(x.source).to.eql(pm.variables.get('filter_source'))));",
                  "pm.test('Date filter', () => j.data.forEach(x => { pm.expect(x.published_at).to.not.eql(null); pm.expect(x.published_at.substring(0, 10) >= pm.variables.get('date_from')).to.eql(true); }));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "03 Search page 2",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{api_key}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/articles/search?page=2&per_page=10"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Page 2', () => pm.expect(j.page).to.eql(2));",
                  "pm.test('No overlap with page 1 (run 01 first; data unchanged)', () => { const ids = JSON.parse(pm.collectionVariables.get('page1_ids') || '[]'); pm.expect(ids.length).to.be.above(0); j.data.forEach(x => pm.expect(ids).to.not.include(x.id)); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "04 Stats",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{api_key}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/articles/stats"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Total equals source sum', () => pm.expect(j.total_articles).to.eql(Object.values(j.by_source).reduce((a,b) => a+b, 0)));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "05 Sales detail",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{api_key}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/attrition/department/Sales"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Sales', () => { pm.expect(j.department).to.eql('Sales'); pm.expect(j.top_earners.length).to.be.at.most(3); pm.expect(j.attrition_rate).to.be.within(0,1); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "06 Risk profile",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{api_key}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/attrition/risk-profile"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Rule checks', () => { pm.expect(j.length).to.be.at.most(20); j.forEach(x => { pm.expect(x.OverTime).to.eql('Yes'); pm.expect(x.YearsAtCompany).to.be.below(3); }); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "1. Public",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Root",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                ""
              ]
            },
            "description": "Public — no auth needed. Returns API info and available paths."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Health Check",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/health",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Public — returns status and server timestamp."
          }
        }
      ],
      "description": "No authentication required."
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Get JWT Token",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "    var json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('jwt_token', json.access_token);",
                  "    pm.test('Token saved to collection variable', function() {",
                  "        pm.expect(json.access_token).to.be.a('string');",
                  "        pm.expect(json.token_type).to.eql('bearer');",
                  "    });",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"client_id\": \"{{client_id}}\",\n    \"client_secret\": \"{{client_secret}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/token",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "token"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Exchange client credentials for a JWT token.\n\nThe test script auto-saves the token to the `jwt_token` collection variable so the JWT folder requests work immediately."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Test — No Auth (should 401)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Returns 401 without auth', function() {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(401);",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/articles/stats",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "articles",
                "stats"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Verify that protected endpoints reject unauthenticated requests."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Test — Wrong API Key (should 401)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Returns 401 with wrong key', function() {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(401);",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "wrong-key-here"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/articles/stats",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "articles",
                "stats"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Verify that invalid API keys are rejected."
          }
        }
      ],
      "description": "Authentication flow and negative tests."
    },
    {
      "name": "3. Articles (ETL) — API Key",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Article Stats (total + per source)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', function() {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Has total and by_source', function() {",
                  "    var json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(json).to.have.property('total_articles');",
                  "    pm.expect(json).to.have.property('by_source');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{api_key}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/articles/stats",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "articles",
                "stats"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Total article count with breakdown per source (bbc, nytimes, books.toscrape, etc)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "List Articles (no filter)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{api_key}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/articles?limit=5",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "articles"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "5"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "List latest 5 articles, no filter."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "List Articles — Filter by Source",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{api_key}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/articles?source=books.toscrape&limit=5",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "articles"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "source",
